  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Instead of always center, please allow the option to use the end point/points of a \"proximity\" contact receiver for calculating the parameter's float(closeness). This would allow existing systems to use less complicated systems for calculation of distance and create new options for determining closeness or distance to an object.\n\nUsage examples that would directly benefit: \n\nSliders - length of a sword, volume of a slider - a lot less contacts and more accurate results.\n\nIn above case, it's always estimated where the middle point is always 1 so not touching would lead to 0 and require more contacts.\n\nTracing specific line movements for activating an effect like drawing a star - here, using less contacts and forcing accurate movement",
